<section class="section reveal" id="azure-landscape">
  <span class="section-label">Fundamentals</span>
  <h2>The Azure AI <span class="accent">Landscape</span></h2>

  <p>Microsoft Azure has invested heavily in AI services, creating a multi-layered ecosystem serving different abstraction levels. At the lowest level, you have pre-built APIs for vision, language, and speech. In the middle, Azure OpenAI provides access to frontier LLMs. At the highest level, Azure Machine Learning offers end-to-end MLOps capabilities for building custom models.</p>

  <p>Understanding where each service fits helps you make architectural decisions balancing time-to-market, customization needs, and cost. Building a real-time vision classification system requires a different approach than fine-tuning a large language model.</p>

  <div class="analogy">
    <h4>💡 Think of It This Way</h4>
    <p>Azure's AI services form a pyramid. At the base, pre-built APIs solve common problems instantly — like adding text translation to your app. As you move up, services become more flexible and customizable but require more expertise. At the peak, custom ML offers maximum control but demands the most effort. Choose based on your problem's specificity and time constraints.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="compare-grid">
    <div class="compare-card">
      <h5>Cognitive Services (APIs)</h5>
      <p>Pre-built, ready-to-use APIs for common AI tasks. No model training required — just call the endpoint.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Vision: OCR, object detection, face recognition</li>
        <li>Language: Text analytics, NER, sentiment analysis</li>
        <li>Speech: Speech-to-text, text-to-speech, translation</li>
        <li>Deployment time: Minutes to hours</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="compare-card">
      <h5>Azure OpenAI (LLMs)</h5>
      <p>Controlled access to frontier LLMs via Azure infrastructure. Full fine-tuning and deployment support.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Models: GPT-4, GPT-3.5-turbo, Embedding models</li>
        <li>Enterprise features: VPC isolation, managed keys, audit logs</li>
        <li>Fine-tuning on custom data</li>
        <li>Deployment time: Hours to days</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="compare-card">
      <h5>Azure Machine Learning (ML Studio)</h5>
      <p>Full-stack MLOps platform for building, training, and deploying custom models at scale.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Experiment tracking and model versioning</li>
        <li>Automated ML (AutoML) for rapid prototyping</li>
        <li>Integrated compute for training</li>
        <li>Deployment time: Days to weeks</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="why-matters">
    <h4>🌍 Why This Matters</h4>
    <p><strong>In Financial AI:</strong> Azure's Cognitive Services offer built-in compliance features for financial data processing. When you need rapid fraud detection or transaction classification, pre-built APIs deploy within hours, meeting tight regulatory timelines.</p>
    <p><strong>In Life Sciences AI:</strong> Azure ML's integration with healthcare datasets and HIPAA compliance features makes it ideal for medical imaging and genomics analysis, where custom models often outperform off-the-shelf solutions.</p>
    <p><strong>In Deep Tech:</strong> Enterprises building proprietary models leverage Azure ML's full MLOps stack, automating retraining pipelines and managing model versioning at scale.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="key-takeaway">
    <h4>✦ Key Takeaways</h4>
    <ul>
      <li>Azure offers three tiers: Cognitive Services, Azure OpenAI, and ML Studio</li>
      <li>Choose based on problem specificity: generic problems benefit from pre-built APIs</li>
      <li>All Azure AI services share common infrastructure: authentication, monitoring, and cost management</li>
      <li>Enterprise features like VPC isolation and audit logging are built-in to all tiers</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

