<section class="section reveal" id="cost-planning">
  <span class="section-label">Practical Considerations</span>
  <h2>Cost Optimization &amp; <span class="accent">Resource Planning</span></h2>

  <p>Azure AI services are billed differently depending on service tier and usage patterns. Cognitive Services charge per API call. Azure OpenAI charges per token. Azure ML charges for compute hours. Understanding these billing models upfront prevents surprise costs and optimizes your architecture.</p>

  <p>A common mistake is deploying services without understanding usage patterns. A chatbot processing 100k messages daily might cost $500/month with Cognitive Services but only $50/month with Azure OpenAI, depending on model choice and token usage.</p>

  <h3>Cost Optimization Strategies</h3>
  <div class="stages">
    <div class="stage-card">
      <div class="stage-num">1</div>
      <div class="stage-content">
        <h4>Right-Size Your Service Tier</h4>
        <p>Azure AI services come in multiple pricing tiers. Standard tier is suitable for most applications. Premium tier includes advanced features like higher quotas and priority support.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="stage-card">
      <div class="stage-num">2</div>
      <div class="stage-content">
        <h4>Use Batch Processing for Non-Real-Time Workloads</h4>
        <p>Batch APIs offer 50% discounts compared to real-time APIs. If your use case allows 24-hour latency, use batch processing.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="stage-card">
      <div class="stage-num">3</div>
      <div class="stage-content">
        <h4>Implement Caching and Rate Limiting</h4>
        <p>Cache API responses for identical requests. Implement rate limiting to prevent runaway costs from bugs or unexpected traffic.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="stage-card">
      <div class="stage-num">4</div>
      <div class="stage-content">
        <h4>Monitor and Alert on Spending</h4>
        <p>Set up Azure Cost Management alerts. Monitor API call volume and set thresholds that trigger notifications when usage increases unexpectedly.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h3>Cost Estimation Example</h3>
  <p>Consider a document processing application processing 10,000 documents daily:</p>

  <div class="code-header"><span class="code-lang">Python</span><button class="copy-btn">Copy</button></div>
  <pre><code><span class="cm"># Cost calculation for Azure AI services</span>
<span class="va">daily_documents</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="nm">10_000</span>
<span class="va">monthly_documents</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="va">daily_documents</span> <span class="op">*</span> <span class="nm">30</span>

<span class="cm"># Azure Computer Vision: $1 per 1000 API calls</span>
<span class="va">vision_cost</span> <span class="op">=</span> (<span class="va">monthly_documents</span> <span class="op">/</span> <span class="nm">1000</span>) <span class="op">*</span> <span class="nm">1.0</span>

<span class="cm"># Azure Text Analytics: $1 per 1000 records</span>
<span class="va">text_cost</span> <span class="op">=</span> (<span class="va">monthly_documents</span> <span class="op">/</span> <span class="nm">1000</span>) <span class="op">*</span> <span class="nm">1.0</span>

<span class="va">total_monthly</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="va">vision_cost</span> <span class="op">+</span> <span class="va">text_cost</span>
<span class="fn">print</span>(<span class="st">f"Monthly cost: $</span>{<span class="va">total_monthly</span>:<span class="st">.2f</span>}<span class="st">"</span>)  <span class="cm"># $600</span></code></pre>
  <div class="code-explain">
    <p><strong>What is happening here:</strong> We calculate monthly cost for running OCR and text analysis on 10,000 documents daily. Both services charge per transaction, making this example predictable for budget planning.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="key-takeaway">
    <h4>✦ Key Takeaways</h4>
    <ul>
      <li>Different services have different billing models — understand them before deploying</li>
      <li>Use batch processing for 50% cost savings on non-real-time workloads</li>
      <li>Set up Azure Cost Management alerts to catch unexpected spending</li>
      <li>Compare service costs against your requirements to optimize your architecture</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

